00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
when elon musk offered to buy twitter  for 54.20 cents a share or 43 billion he  said he was not playing the back and  forth game he was moving straight to the  end and this was his best and final  offer in the securities and exchange  commission filing a twitter's board  tried to stop him in his tracks by  adopting a so-called poison pill to make  it harder for musk to buy the company  under the structure shareholders are  allowed to purchase newly offered shares  at a discount except for the person  trying to acquire the company in this  case musk he'd have to purchase the new  shares at a higher price so it's a  measure to stop him from taking over  more shares of the platform as soon as  he hits 15  he currently owns 9  musk is said to be fighting back with a  plan of his own he is reportedly  speaking with investors who could  partner with him in his bid for twitter  one option according to the new york  post is to team up with private equity  firm silver lake's co-ceo egon durbin a  twitter board member who led musk's  effort to take tesla private the tesla  ceo is apparently also threatening to  appeal directly to shareholders he sent  out a cryptic tweet over the weekend  love me tender in reference to an elvis  presley song it could mean that he'll  bypass the board and invite shareholders  to sell or tender their stock to him at  a premium so they'll make a lot of money  what does he want with twitter in any  case i mean the guy already builds  electric cars and envisions trips to  mars given his professed mission to save  the world it may actually make sense if  his goal is to save the world in one way  or another he sees his purchase of  twitter as a way of saving democracy he  feels twitter is not living up to its  promise of being a platform for free  speech which he calls a societal  imperative for a functioning democracy  in the sec filing he said at a recent  ted event that a good way to tell if  free speech exists is to ask this  question is someone you don't like  allowed to say something you don't like  in the past few years twitter has  started fact checking and suspending  accounts it most famously banned donald  trump over his tweets surrounding the  2021 capital riots musk's patience with  twitter apparently ran out when it  suspended the account of new satire site  the babylon b which named u.s assistant  secretary for health dr rachel levine  its man of the year after usa today  named the transgender official one of  its women of the year babylon b's ceo  seth dillon said musk reached out to  confirm their account had in fact been  suspended dylan said musk even mused on  that call that he might need to buy  twitter purchasing his go-to social  media platform is certainly easier than  starting his own app which he says he  has seriously considered so what would  twitter look like under a new ownership  will the former president be welcomed  back we'll have to see during the recent  ted interview musk suggested bans should  be done with caution and that timeouts  are better than banning people  permanently he suggested that when it  comes to determining whether offensive  tweets should be removed the policy  should always be to let it stay when in  doubt so when in doubt leave it in don't  take it out musk has criticized  twitter's secret algorithm which it uses  to decide what to show you on your feed  he said the algorithm should be open  sourced so the public can inspect the  underlying code behind the algorithm to  ensure there's no manipulation behind  the scenes so basically you'd know  whether something was done to promote or  demote a tweet he wants an edit button  so people can revise their comments and  also wants to eliminate spam bots and  scam bots under his leadership ads could  be a thing of the past he has taken aim  at twitter's revenue model which relies  on advertising not everyone is happy  about an elon musk takeover including  some twitter employees and a saudi  prince and twitter shareholder musk shot  back by asking for the saudi arabian  kingdom's views on free speech the  country is known to crack down on  freedom of expression others were  reportedly already worried about him  joining the board let alone buying  twitter musk abruptly canceled his plans  to join the company's board which is  made up of the current twitter ceo barak  agrawal former ceo and co-founder jack  dorsey and independent directors in the  sec filing he stated i don't have  confidence in management a former sec  chair explained that joining the board  could have limited his influence jay  clayton told cnbc when you go on the  board of directors of a company your  degrees of freedom as an investor are  substantially restricted so instead of  joining the board he decided he wanted  to buy the whole shebang twitter has  over 200 million daily users two-thirds  of the size of the us population some of  its users have been described as woke an  ideology musk has blasted in an  interview with the babylon bee he said  wokeness basically wants to make comedy  illegal which is not cool trying to shut  down chappelle come on man that's crazy  he's referencing the attempt to cancel  comedian dave chappelle over transgender  remarks in his netflix special he  continued do you want a humorless  society that is simply rife with  condemnation and hate basically at his  heart wokeness is divisive exclusionary  and hateful it basically gives mean  people a shield to be mean and cruel  armored in false virtue while musk is  presenting himself as the king of free  speech others accuse him of hypocrisy in  february tesla employee john bernal said  he was fired from his job after posting  reviews critical of tesla's full  self-driving software on his youtube  channel ai addict in 2018 a blogger who  wrote not so flattering articles about  tesla said musk threatened to sue if he  continued writing articles so critics  don't see the richest man in the world  as a savior of free speech by the way  how on earth will he pay for it most of  his money is tied up in tesla stock  although he recently sold billions of  dollars worth of shares he had to pay  billions in taxes and he gave billions  to charity musk hired morgan stanley as  an advisor for the bid according to the  regulatory filing banks are often  brought on board to help with debt  financing having already become the  rocket man an electric car entrepreneur  a builder of tunnels and brain computer  chips he appears determined to be a  social media mogul as well he already  has the best and brightest engineers at  his disposal if twitter needed more  engineering chops if you'd like to brush  up on your science computer science and  math skills my sponsor brilliant has an  incredible website and app that makes  learning stem fun and it's super  interactive you can learn the key ideas  of computer science with their computer  science fundamentals course and no  coding is required it's great if you're  in high school or college and want to  learn the fundamentals or if you've  started your career and you like to  brush up on what you already know and if  you get the incorrect answer you can  click on the explanations to see where  you went wrong there's something for  everyone on brilliant including the  super fun logic courses that are my  personal favorite they really help  strengthen your analytical muscles to  get started for free visit brilliant.org  newsthink or click on the link in my  description or pin comment and the first  200 of you to click my link will get 20  off brilliant annual premium  subscription which unlocks all of the  courses thanks for watching for  newsthink i'm cindy  palm you

